{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>This is the law of the sin-offering.</b> And it calls it קדש קדשים (most holy) like the meal-offering, and likewise the law of the guilt-offering that it mentions after it, it calls קדש קדשים. And this is the arrangement of the sections: it mentioned first the section of the burnt-offering, and after it the section of the meal-offering, and after it the section of the sin-offering, and after it the section of the guilt-offering, and called them all קדש קדשים. And this is what Scripture says after arranging the sections: ״זאת התורה לעולה למנחה ולחטאת ולאשם״ — 'This is the law for the burnt-offering, for the meal-offering, and for the sin-offering, and for the guilt-offering' (Leviticus 7:37). And it wanted to explain first the laws of קדשי קדשים (most holy offerings), for they share one rule, and afterwards it explains the laws of קדשים קלים (lesser holy offerings), such as peace-offerings and the thank-offering." "<b>In the place where the burnt-offering is slaughtered, the sin-offering shall be slaughtered.</b> Now the burnt-offering is slaughtered in the north, and it comes on account of the stirring of the heart, as was stated above. And in order that the sinner not be put to shame, Scripture cautioned that the sin-offering, which comes for a sin of deed, be slaughtered in the very same place where the burnt-offering is slaughtered — so that people would not perceive from this, when he brings his offering, whether he sinned in thought or in deed."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:27.658241987Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}